WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.380
A student images one stretched dish and one unstretched dish.

2
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.040
The student scores 600 cells in each.

3
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:17.260
The difference has a p-value below 0.0001.

4
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.240
How many experiments is that?

5
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:27.840
One. Every cell in the stretched dish shared the same dish, the same pipetting, and

6
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:28.840
the same afternoon.

7
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:34.220
If that dish was odd, all 600 cells carry the oddity together.

8
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.580
Here is the rule. The thing you independently assign to a treatment is the

9
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.820
experimental unit.

10
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.920
It can be a dish, a stretch device, or a mouse.

11
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.740
The thing you measure is the observational unit.

12
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:56.400
It can be a cell. N, the sample size, is the number of experimental units.

13
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.500
Add a drug to a whole well, and the well is the unit.

14
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.400
Measuring more cells adds observational units.

15
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.740
It adds no experimental units.

16
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:11.010
Here is a made-up data set, invented for teaching.

17
00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.350
Three independent runs, on different days.

18
00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:18.590
Each run has one control dish and one treated dish.

19
00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.750
Two hundred cells are scored in each dish for EdU.

20
00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:27.890
It is a thymidine analogue that cells build into DNA as they replicate it.

21
00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:29.890
Now pool the cells.

22
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:40.790
Control is 120 of 600, 20%. Treated is 178 of 600, 29.7%.

23
00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:46.170
Treat each cell as independent, and the standard error is about 2.5 points.

24
00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.710
Then z is about 3.9.

25
00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:50.310
It looks decisive.

26
00:01:51.233 --> 00:01:53.553
That analysis counted cells.

27
00:01:54.493 --> 00:01:56.253
Now make the dish the unit.

28
00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.153
Each run pairs its two dishes.

29
00:02:00.073 --> 00:02:03.773
The differences are 14, 2, and 13 points.

30
00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:06.533
The mean is 9.67.

31
00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:11.713
The spread between runs gives a standard error of 3.84.

32
00:02:12.493 --> 00:02:14.433
That is larger than 2.5.

33
00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:20.713
The 95% interval runs from minus 6.9 to 26.2 points.

34
00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:24.867
So the effect is suggestive, not shown.

35
00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:29.467
The interval runs from a small decrease to a large increase.

36
00:02:30.287 --> 00:02:33.027
The p-value is about 0.13.

37
00:02:33.747 --> 00:02:35.867
That does not show no effect.

38
00:02:36.947 --> 00:02:39.627
Scoring 2,000 cells per dish would not help.

39
00:02:40.327 --> 00:02:43.227
The uncertainty comes from run-to-run variation.

40
00:02:43.227 --> 00:02:45.607
More independent runs would.

41
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:50.110
A SuperPlot shows all this in one figure.

42
00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:54.610
Each run's mean is a large symbol, colored by run.

43
00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:58.010
The comparison uses the large symbols.

44
00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.870
Run 2 stands out at once.

45
00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.430
It is the run where treatment barely moved the mean.

46
00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:10.470
Keep the rule. N is the number of independent runs, not the number of cells.
